sse-keepalive is an HTTP/1.1 reverse proxy that keeps Server-Sent Events
streams alive across long provider silences, such as the multi-minute prompt
prefill of llama.cpp on large prompts. Clients with stall watchdogs (Zed,
ACP agents) otherwise cancel a healthy request.

It relays traffic verbatim and, on streaming completions only, asks the
provider for native progress, emits a structurally valid empty chunk at
stream start and again whenever the provider is silent for the configured
cadence. Clients that opt in via X-Keepalive-Protocol receive labelled
frames with prefill progress and ETA.

FreeBSD-native: kqueue event loops, one worker process per CPU with a
thread-per-core option, SO_REUSEPORT_LB accept balancing, accf_data accept
filters, supervised workers with rolling restart on SIGHUP.
